                        <tr>
                           <th>Conclusion and Recommendations based on this report and previous findings known to us:</th>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>Renal function is within normal limits (eGFR 80 mL/min/1.73 m²). Urine albumin/creatinine ratio is at the upper limit of normal (29 mg/g), suggesting no significant albuminuria but close to the threshold for microalbuminuria. Continued monitoring of renal function and urinary albumin is recommended, especially considering the patient’s age.</td>
